Most stages in [[The Battle Cats]] yield some kind of reward for players who have cleared them.

When the player obtains a stage reward, a special pop-up box will appear during the stage clear result screen.

[[File:Stage Reward.png|thumb|centre|400px|Stage clear screen with reward pop-up below the XP result]]

==Kinds of reward==
There are a few different kinds of reward available in the game:

*[[Ototo Corps|Ototo Materials]]
*Clear Bonus: when clearing the final stage of a map for the first time the player receives 30 [[Cat Food]] and a [[Leadership]].
*Normal stage rewards: the stage has a certain amount of rewards available, and the player can obtain any one of those rewards.
*[[Treasure]]: only available in [[Empire of Cats]], [[Into the Future]], and [[Cats of the Cosmos]]. They offer various permanent upgrades to players.
*[[Timed Score Reward]]: the player can obtain multiple rewards from the same stage, and how many rewards they obtain depends on how fast they cleared the stage.
*Unlock rewards: clearing the stage fulfills a certain condition, which offers a permanent reward of some kind. Examples include:
**Various cats that can be unlocked after clearing certain [[Empire of Cats]] stages, such as [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]], [[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)|Ninja Cat]] and [[Moneko (Special Cat)|Moneko]].
**[[Gamatoto Expedition]] after clearing [[Greece (Empire of Cats)|Greece]] in the first chapter of [[Empire of Cats]].
**[[Legend Stages]] after clearing the first chapter of Empire of Cats.
**Units/True Forms unlocked from clearing floors 30/40/50 of [[Heavenly Tower|Heavenly]]/[[Infernal Tower]] (via [[Catnip Challenges]]).
**All rewards from [[An Ancient Curse]] (besides the 380,000 XP and Treasure Radar, which are normal stage rewards).

Since these rewards are all separated, a stage can drop any number of different types of rewards. In practice, there are no examples of stages that have both Treasure and normal stage rewards, so sometimes normal stage rewards can be referred to as "treasure".

==Normal Rewards==
A maximum of one normal reward can be obtained upon clearing a stage. A stage can have multiple drops available, each with their own set chances. Currently, there are 5 types of normal stage reward:

*Reward type 1: the first drop can only drop once, but all subsequent drops can drop infinitely. Used on stages like [[Merciless XP!]] (with [[#Reward Reset|one important caveat]]), many SoL stages, and [[Cat Capsule#Lucky Capsules G|Lucky Ticket G]] stages.
*Reward type 0: all drops can drop infinitely. Used on most stages.
*Reward type -1: unclear, but seems to be similar to reward type 0.
*Reward type -3: a reward is guaranteed to be dropped once. Treasure Radars cannot be used. Used in [[Infernal Tower]].
*Reward type -4: same as -3, but rewards can drop infinitely. Used in [[Builder's Blitz Stages]].

Certain stages will drop cat units or cat unit True Forms, such as [[The Great Escaper]] or [[:Category:Awakening Stages|Awakening Stages]]. These drops can only be obtained once, even if their reward type would otherwise have them drop infinitely.

==Reward Reset==
When a map resets (either by the event ending or by hitting its maximum amount of clears), it can sometimes reset the rewards. While most stages do nothing on reset, some may do the following:

*Reset the reward drop status. Notably, this is used on [[Merciless XP!]] and [[XP Bonanza!]]; these stages have reward type 1, but because they reset immediately after clearing they effectively have reward type 0.
*Reset the reward drop status and map clearance. Used in many stages, such as Gauntlets, the Towers, and most limited events (especially collabs).
*Reset the maximum amount of clears. Used in [[Behemoth Culling]], [[The Proving Grounds]], and [[Catamin Stages]].

